-- Gameplay v2 catalogue: 100 weekly challenges, twenty per tier, and a pool of 21 daily ones.
--
-- Written from docs/CHALLENGES-CATALOGUE.md, under the rules of docs/CHALLENGES.md:
--
--   * Competitive is required by the hardest tier only. Everything below it filters on
--     COMPETITIVE_OR_UNRATED, so a player who never queues ranked can still validate four weekly
--     challenges out of five and every daily one.
--   * Nothing can be destroyed by a single bad match. Streaks (MAX_STREAK) and rates held across
--     the week (RATIO) are gone; the same questions are asked as COUNT_MATCHES, where missing one
--     match costs that match and nothing else.
--   * Agents are capped at three, in both directions.
--   * Every number is a base target for the squad the catalogue was calibrated on (reference
--     5 300). The draw scales it to the campaign in force and stores the result on the selection.
--   * A daily challenge is decided in one or two matches, never requires Competitive, and has no
--     difficulty: it is its own tier.
--
-- The old catalogue is deleted rather than converted: 61 of its 70 entries survive here under new
-- codes, filters and targets, and V40 already dropped every row that referenced it.
--
-- Exclusion groups share a name across tiers when two entries ask the same question, so one weekly
-- pack never asks it twice.

DELETE FROM challenge;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;
